A||||13||Phantom Rage||A quick fuel/boost question?||||5||
Z||000000||Phantom Rage||04-19-2001||08:24 PM||||Is one extra psi of fuel per pound of boost enough to keep a motor from going lean?  Given a turbo’s efficiency to produce 550cfm @ 15psi.  <P>I know there are a lot more factors to consider, but I am just curious in the general sense.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||gixxer||04-19-2001||09:52 PM||||With the stock computer injector pulse duration, I'd guess with 75 PSI total fuel pressure, that you could only support about 200 HP.<BR>This is pretty rough 'tho, and assuming 19 lb/hr injectors are stock.<BR>I'm assuming that the stock injectors are only flowing enough fuel for 140 HP, about 12.5 lb/hr each, and adding the extra flow capacity only from the extra pressure 30 PSI(15 PSI from the stocker, and 15 PSI extra from a aftermarket unit in series), not from a reprogrammed chip.<BR>Needless to say with 15 PSI boost, you could be making 230 HP or so with a stock 2.8, so<BR>your engine would probably roast.<BR>Anybody else; feel free to correct this post.<BR>Thanx<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phantom Rage||04-20-2001||01:48 AM||||Thanks Gizzer that was very informative, but I was referring to the Iron Duke.  Sorry, I know that I should have made that clear.  I know 15 psi is way too much for the little duke, it is just what my upgraded turbo is rated at.  I am asking because I may be on to something, but don’t want to raise any hopes just yet.  Like I said, I just need to know in general if that sounds feasible, give hypothetically that everything else has been worked out.  <P>Once again thanks Gixxer!<P>Does any else know?  <BR>||||reg||7
